## When to use

- A setting that takes effect immediately: public/private, alerts on/off, a feature
  flag.
- A row in a settings list, where the label describes the thing and the switch
  describes its state.
- A preference with no submit button. Flipping it saves.

## When not to use

- The change is only applied on submit; use `checkbox`, which is the familiar form
  control for a pending decision.
- One of several options; use `radio-group`.
- A formatting command on a selection; use `toggle`.

## API

| Prop              | Type                        | Default     | Description                                    |
| ----------------- | --------------------------- | ----------- | ---------------------------------------------- |
| `checked`         | `boolean`                   | –           | Controlled state.                              |
| `defaultChecked`  | `boolean`                   | `false`     | Uncontrolled initial state.                    |
| `onCheckedChange` | `(checked, details) => void`| –           | Fired on click and on Space.                   |
| `size`            | `"sm" \| "default"`         | `"default"` | Track and thumb scale.                         |
| `disabled`        | `boolean`                   | `false`     | Ignores interaction and form submission.       |
| `readOnly`        | `boolean`                   | `false`     | Focusable, submitted, not changeable.          |
| `required`        | `boolean`                   | `false`     | Blocks submit until switched on.               |
| `name`, `value`   | `string`                    | –           | Form field identity and submitted value.       |
| `className`       | `string` / state callback                    | –           | Merged last.                                   |

## Motion contract

Authored intensity is **subtle**: The thumb travels only within its measured track, the track and the thumb each own one scoped palette, and an explicit size revision remeasures the endpoint.

The thumb is the protagonist. It travels between two measured endpoints — the
distance is read from the track and the thumb, never written down — while the
track and the thumb each run one state paint transaction. Nothing else in the
control moves.

| Recipe / form | Owner and full behaviour | reduced | none |
| ------------- | ------------------------ | ------- | ---- |
| `data.transition/one-shot` | One opacity entrance on a switch inserted into an already-presented page. A presenting parent (such as an entering field), a hidden or unusable control and an already-visible switch keep native paint, and the thumb never sweeps in. | Short opacity. | Immediate. |
| `state.morph/one-shot` | The thumb's own endpoint revision: the measured travel with a non-overshooting indicator spring. The first measurement and a passive font/viewport/caller-layout change paint the endpoint immediately, and a rapid toggle retargets the same thumb host. | Position immediately. | Position immediately. |
| `state.color/css-transition` | The track's background, border and focus-ring paint on one clock, and the thumb's own fill on its own host. Real DOM focus and a palette we cannot prove settle all of that paint at its target. | Short eligible colour. | Zero duration and delay. |
| `geometry.resize/measured` | An explicit `size` change interpolates the measured track box. The thumb endpoint is remeasured from the same change and held to the interval that stays valid through the whole transaction, then painted at the exact measured endpoint. | Final geometry immediately. | Final geometry immediately. |

Under `reduced` the thumb still ends up in the right place: position is state, not
decoration. What is dropped is the travel animation and the size interpolation.
Under `none` the thumb, the track box and every colour reach their target with
zero duration and delay. A native form reset stays Base UI's own path: Cadence
adds no callback, revision or replay for it.

## Keyboard interactions

| Keys    | Action                                  |
| ------- | --------------------------------------- |
| `Tab`   | Moves focus to the switch.              |
| `Space` | Toggles the switch, unless `readOnly`.  |
| `Enter` | Toggles with the default Base UI keyboard handling, unless `readOnly`. |

## Accessibility

- Base UI renders `role="switch"` with `aria-checked` and a hidden input, so the
  value is submitted with the form.
- The state is not carried by colour alone: the thumb position, the track colour,
  and `aria-checked` change together.
- Give it a name with `Label htmlFor` or `aria-label`. "On" is a state, not a name.
- A switch that saves immediately should announce the outcome (a `toast` or an
  inline status), because there is no submit step to confirm it.

## Validation and data ownership

| The component does                              | You do                                          |
| ------------------------------------------------ | ----------------------------------------------- |
| Forwards `name`, `value`, `disabled`, `required` | Persisting the setting and handling failures     |
| Forwards supplied `aria-invalid`                   | Deciding whether the switch needs one at all     |
| Renders the on/off state                         | Announcing that the change was saved             |

Invalid semantics do not add a destructive track style; supply a visible error message when needed.
There is no `validate` or `schema` prop. [Field](/components/field) shows how the invalid state
and its message are wired.

## Responsive behavior

The control is fixed-size at every breakpoint; the row around it is what changes.
In a narrow layout, let the label and description wrap above the switch instead of
shrinking the track.

## Performance

One `ResizeObserver` pair per switch measures the track and the thumb, so a font
or layout change does not desynchronise the endpoint; an owned size writer is
excluded from that read. The animation itself is a single `transform`
transition, one scoped colour family on the track and one on the thumb, plus one
measured width/height transaction when the `size` prop changes. No layout read
happens during interaction.

## Notes for AI

- Use `switch` only for immediate settings. If there is a Save button, use
  `checkbox`.
- The track and thumb colours are one scoped state transaction, not decorative
  motion; do not add a second colour writer or animate unrelated properties.
- Keep the label outside the switch. A switch with no label has no accessible name.
